---
import ComponentPage from '../../layouts/component-page.astro';

const html = `<p>Beans ship the day after roasting. <a class="nib-link" href="#content">Read the roast schedule</a>.</p>

<p class="text-tags">
  <span class="nib-tag nib-tag--green">New</span>
  <span class="nib-tag nib-tag--red">Sale</span>
  <span class="nib-tag">Draft</span>
  <span class="nib-tag nib-tag--yellow nib-tag--filled">Low stock</span>
  <span class="nib-tag nib-tag--accent">Live</span>
</p>

<div class="nib-callout nib-callout--note">
  <p class="nib-callout__label">Note</p>
  <p>Grind just before brewing; ground coffee goes flat in a day.</p>
</div>

<div class="nib-callout nib-callout--error" role="alert">
  <p class="nib-callout__label">Error</p>
  <p>The card was declined. Nothing was charged.</p>
  <div class="nib-callout__actions">
    <button class="nib-button nib-button--outline" type="button">Try another card</button>
  </div>
</div>

<figure class="nib-code">
  <figcaption class="nib-code__header">
    install.sh
    <button class="nib-button nib-button--ghost" data-nib="copy" type="button">Copy</button>
  </figcaption>
  <pre tabindex="0"><code><span class="nib-syntax-keyword">pnpm</span> add @nib-ui/css <span class="nib-syntax-string">"@nib-ui/js"</span> <span class="nib-syntax-comment"># ${'-'}-save-exact</span></code></pre>
</figure>`;

const js = `<script type="module">
  import '@nib-ui/js/copy';
  import { init } from '@nib-ui/js';
  init();
</script>`;
---

<ComponentPage
  title="Text"
  lead="The inline and block pieces of running text: links, tags, callouts and code blocks with a COPY button."
  kind="CSS"
  code={{ html: `${html}\n\n${js}` }}
>
  <div slot="example" class="text-example" set:html={html} />

  <h2>Usage</h2>
  <p>
    <code>nib-link</code> is an ink link with a line-coloured underline; <code>aria-current="page"</code> gives it an
    accent underline. <code>nib-tag</code> takes a hue modifier (<code>--blue</code> … <code>--red</code>,
    <code>--accent</code> for current states only) and <code>--filled</code> for status chips. <code>nib-callout</code>
    takes a tone (<code>--note</code>, <code>--warning</code>, <code>--error</code>, <code>--done</code>,
    <code>--next</code>) that sets the hue and the glyph before its label.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>nib-code</code> wraps a <code>pre</code>; colour tokens with <code>nib-syntax-keyword</code>,
    <code>-string</code>, <code>-number</code>, <code>-identifier</code> and <code>-comment</code> spans. Import
    <code>@nib-ui/js/copy</code> and a <code>data-nib="copy"</code> button copies the block, reads
    <code>Copied ✓</code> for two seconds and announces it. <code>data-copied-label</code> and
    <code>data-failed-label</code> set the words in your language; <code>data-copy-target</code> copies another element
    by id.
  </p>

  <ul slot="accessibility">
    <li>
      A tag's hue never carries meaning alone: the word does. Callout glyphs are decoration; the label word is read.
    </li>
    <li>
      Give an error callout <code>role="alert"</code> when it appears after an action, so it is announced; other tones
      need no role.
    </li>
    <li>
      A scrolling code block needs <code>tabindex="0"</code> so keyboard users can scroll it. COPY announces the result
      in a polite live region (a failure, assertively); the tick is hidden from screen readers.
    </li>
    <li>Link text says where it goes; mark an external link with ↗ in its text.</li>
  </ul>
</ComponentPage>

<script>
  import '@nib-ui/js/copy';
  import { init } from '@nib-ui/js';
  init();
</script>

<style>
  .text-example > :global(* + *) {
    margin-block-start: var(--nib-space-lg);
  }

  .text-example :global(.text-tags) {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--nib-space-md);
  }
</style>
